    "result_text": "Build is green \u2014 both tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key to be the SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, and made duplicate/soft-match detection follow from it. Changes were kept to small, low-complexity units:\n\n**New file \u2014 `Soundex.java`**: A self-contained American Soundex utility (`Soundex.of(name)`). Isolating the phonetic algorithm here keeps it out of the two edited classes, so neither of their existing methods pays for its complexity.\n\n**`IdentityKey.java`**:\n- `forRequest` / `forOwner` now feed `lastName` (not the computed `householdId`) into the key.\n- `key(...)` now hashes `E164(telephone) | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)` with SHA-256, producing the 64-hex value the test asserts.\n- Extracted a full `sha256Hex` and made the existing `sha256Hex12` (still used by `household()`) delegate to it; removed the now-unused `orEmpty`.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`**: The soft match now triggers when the `identityKey` differs but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` both match \u2014 so household members with different telephones become a soft match rather than a hard 409.\n\nBehaviour that was already correct, left untouched:\n- **409 duplicate detection** (`RejectDuplicateIdentity`) already compares full identity keys and ignores deleted owners; it now uses the new key automatically.\n- **Email-domain blocklist first**: `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (the disposable-domain block) already runs earlier in the `owners.POST` pipeline than the duplicate check.\n- **Household 409 no longer applies**: `RejectDuplicateHousehold` was already absent from the create pipeline; only its escalation handler yaml lingers as dead wiring.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
